 ## Command path
 
+Panic contexts leave UFS logging to the normal writer's last completed
+records. Media I/O uses driver-owned slot buffers so timeout cannot leave a
+DMA reference to a caller's memory. An uncertain completion quarantines the
+transport until reboot and refuses queued slot requests.
+
 Up to 32 commands run at once, one per command slot. The request list sits on
 a write-combined page of its own, so slot s uses list entry s; without that page
 16 slots use the even entries of the DMA region, so no two entries share a cache
@@ -53,7 +58,7 @@ on two lanes in FAST mode, as the boot firmware leaves it.
